Article 2 (Mutual Aid Regulations) The mutual aid regulations shall state the following matters pursuant to Article 6-2 (1) of the Korea Shipping Association Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Act"): <Amended on August 5, 2011; November 30, 2016>
1. Methods of implementing each category of mutual aid business;
2. Terms and conditions of mutual aid contracts;
3. The following matters concerning mutual aid premiums:
  (a) Receipt and refund of mutual aid premiums;
  (b) Methods of calculating premium rates;
  (c) Collection of mutual aid premiums;
4. The following matters concerning mutual aid benefits:
  (a) Recognition, accumulation, and management of liability reserves and extraordinary risk reserves;
  (b) Payment of mutual aid benefits;
5. The objectives of the mutual aid business;
6. Persons and property covered by mutual aid and the scope of its implementation;
7. Limits on and eligibility for mutual aid membership;
8. Organizations responsible for managing the mutual aid business;
9. Reports of maritime distress and payment of rescue expenses;
10. Investigations and directions necessary for carrying out the mutual aid business;
11. Methods of determining standards for assessing the value of vessels;
12. Expenses necessary for carrying out the mutual aid business;
13. Establishment and operation of the Mutual Aid Dispute Deliberation Committee within the Korea Shipping Association;
14. Other matters necessary for operating the mutual aid business.
